    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Twin pregnancy, dichorionic diamniotic (O30.041)</content>. Blood pressure 114/72 mmHg, urine protein negative, and no symptoms of preeclampsia after the missed visit. Concordant growth (8 percent) with normal fluid and Doppler; twin A cephalic, twin B breech. Hemoglobin 11.0 g/dL; platelets 226. EPDS 6 with item 10 scored 0. Weight gain 12.5 kg so far, on track. [S]<list><item>Tdap given today.</item><item>Visits every two weeks until 36 weeks, then weekly, with blood pressure and urine protein each time; growth scan at 36 to 37 weeks.</item><item>Group B streptococcus swab at 36 to 37 weeks; RSV vaccine at 36 weeks, once the season begins in September.</item><item>Weekly fetal heart rate testing from 36 weeks, which can be offered for twins.</item><item>Continue aspirin until delivery.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Delivery plan</content>. For uncomplicated dichorionic twins, birth is recommended at 38 0/7 to 38 6/7 weeks. With twin A head down, vaginal birth is reasonable whatever twin B&apos;s position, with a clinician experienced in breech extraction or internal version; cesarean if twin A is not head down. Twins raise the risk of postpartum hemorrhage. [S]<list><item>She chose induction at 38 weeks 0 days at the hospital, which has a neonatal intensive care unit.</item><item>Epidural advised early in labor; birth in the operating room with the team ready for a cesarean for twin B if needed.</item><item>Active management of the third stage with oxytocin and quantitative blood loss.</item><item>Antenatal corticosteroids only if birth before 34 weeks is threatened.</item><item>She will arrange for her household to take her to the hospital at any hour.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Blood pressure and urine protein</td><td>Every prenatal visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>114/72 mmHg; urine protein negative</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Prenatal visit and growth scan at 29 weeks</td><td>Every four weeks for growth scans; visits every two weeks from 28 weeks</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Missed: the 29-week visit and growth scan did not take place because the scan request was not sent and the cancelled visit was not rebooked. No harm found today: blood pressure 114/72 mmHg, no proteinuria, no symptoms, and concordant growth with normal fluid on today&apos;s scan. Corrective action: all remaining visits and the 36-week scan were booked together today, and the clinic is reviewing how scan requests are linked to visits</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Fetal hearts and fundal height</td><td>Every prenatal visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Fetal hearts 140 and 136 per minute; fundal height 38 cm</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight gain (about 17 to 25 kg for twins from a normal BMI)</td><td>Every prenatal visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>70.5 kg, up 12.5 kg since intake</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Growth scan with discordance</td><td>Every four weeks from about 20 to 24 weeks in a dichorionic twin pregnancy</td><td>Completed today</td><td>2050 and 1890 g; discordance 8 percent; normal fluid and Doppler; twin A cephalic, twin B breech</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Hemoglobin and ferritin</td><td>At intake, at the anatomy-scan visit, at 24 to 28 weeks, and in the third trimester</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Hemoglobin 11.0 g/dL; platelets 226</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Perinatal mood screen (EPDS)</td><td>Each trimester</td><td>Completed today</td><td>6; item 10 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Tdap vaccine</td><td>Once at 27 to 36 weeks in every pregnancy</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Given today</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>RSV vaccine</td><td>At 32 to 36 weeks from September to January</td><td>Due</td><td>At the 36-week visit in September</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Group B streptococcus culture</td><td>At 36 0/7 to 37 6/7 weeks</td><td>Due</td><td>At the 36-week visit</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weekly antenatal fetal testing</td><td>May be considered from 36 0/7 weeks in uncomplicated dichorionic twins</td><td>Due</td><td>From 36 weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Low-dose aspirin</td><td>Daily from 12 weeks until delivery; review at every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Taken nightly; continue until delivery</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Delivery timing and place</td><td>Agreed by 34 weeks</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Induction at 38 weeks 0 days at the hospital with a neonatal intensive care unit</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Preterm labor warning signs</td><td>Every prenatal visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Occasional painless evening tightenings only; warning signs reviewed</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>The cause of the large uterus and the dating of the pregnancy established at the 11-week scan. Outcome by 2026-03-17: Dichorionic diamniotic twins; dating by her last period confirmed by the crown-rump lengths [S]</item><item>An informed choice about aneuploidy screening by 14 weeks. Outcome by 2026-03-17: Chose nuchal translucency for each twin with cell-free DNA; declined diagnostic testing for now [S]</item><item>Hemoglobin and ferritin in the normal range for pregnancy by the third trimester. Outcome by 2026-08-18: Ferritin 31 ng/mL at 25 weeks; hemoglobin 11.0 g/dL at 33 weeks [S]</item><item>Growth discordance under 20 percent at every growth scan. Outcome by 2026-08-18: Discordance 5 percent at 25 weeks and 8 percent at 33 weeks [S]</item><item>A written delivery plan agreed by 34 weeks. Outcome by 2026-08-18: Planned birth at 38 weeks 0 days in the hospital, with a vaginal birth while twin A is head down, an epidural, and the operating room ready [S]</item></list><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Tdap vaccine in pregnancy, 33 weeks [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Multifetal Gestations: Twin, Triplet, and Higher-Order Multifetal Pregnancies: ACOG Practice Bulletin, Number 231 (2021); Medically Indicated Late-Preterm and Early-Term Deliveries: ACOG Committee Opinion, Number 831 (2021); Prediction and Prevention of Spontaneous Preterm Birth: ACOG Practice Bulletin, Number 234 (2021); Aspirin Use to Prevent Preeclampsia and Related Morbidity and Mortality: Preventive Medication (2021); Screening and Diagnosis of Mental Health Conditions During Pregnancy and Postpartum: ACOG Clinical Practice Guideline No. 4 (2023); Guidelines for Vaccinating Pregnant Persons (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Prenatal visits every two weeks until 36 weeks, then weekly; growth scan at 36 to 37 weeks; induction at 38 weeks 0 days. [S]</paragraph></text>

